the falley refinery in southampton it's  the largest in the country usually  receiving oil from all over the world  including russia  but that is changing  vladimir putin over the last  years has been like a pusher  feeding an addiction  in western countries to his hydrocarbons  to his oil and gas  we need to  get ourselves off that addiction that's  why the prime minister is heading to  saudi arabia one of the world's largest  oil producers to discuss alternative  supplies despite concerns over human  rights issues it is politically awkward  but it must be done the uk gets around  eight percent of its oil and four  percent of its gas from russia  boris johnson has promised to end those  oil imports by the end of the year and  dramatically reduce dependence on that  gas  so now he has to find a way to plug that  gap  as a result when the government sets out  its new british energy security strategy  there's likely to be a renewed focus on  drilling in the north sea the fact is  that our economy is overwhelmingly  fossil fuel based so we are going to  burn a lot of fossil fuels for quite a  long time to come  and in the transition  where the renewables which are  incredibly important are intermittent  something's got to back them up  but it's not just about more fossil  fuels as the uk's energy mix from last  month illustrates  nuclear power made up 14.4 percent and  renewables wind hydro and solar combined  made up nearly 45.  what's important about this moment is  that we set ourselves a course as fast  as possible to get to zero emissions as  fast as possible to take ourselves out  of the problems that fossil fuels cause  fossil fuels cause air pollution they  cause climate change they're driving  conflict as part of its new strategy the  government is going to make commitments  to renewables and nuclear power viewed  as the only long-term way to help reduce  energy prices increase energy security  and tackle climate change  but these things will take time to ramp  up and so for the moment there is little  choice no fossil fuel from russia means  difficult choices about where else to  get it  hannah thomas peter sky news in  southampton
 

